Experimental Design and Operation
The experiment was conducted with 3 L glass bottle reactors for 10 days. MBM and RB were mixed at 4:1 ratio on dry weight basis. The moisture content of substrate was adjusted approximately to 60%, and the total weight of substrate in each bottle was 1 kg. The substrate was provided to BSFL for different batch feeding times (5, 4, 3, 2 and 1 time) in each bottle (Table 2). Based on preliminary trials, 1500 3-day-old BSFL were put into 3 L glass bottle. The experiment was carried out in a greenhouse at 27 °C and 60–70% humidity. All treatments in this experiment were replicated three times.
Measurement of Greenhouse Gas and NH3 Emission
The CO2, CH4, N2O, and NH3 samples were daily detected.
GHG samples were collected from the headspace of each glass bottle reactor using 50-mL polypropylene syringe through the rubber tube fitted to a three-way valve, as described in previous study [14]. The collected gas samples were instantly transferred into 12-mL pre-evacuated white-cap flat-bottom glass vials (Labco Exetainer, Labco Limited, UK 839 W) for subsequent measurement of CH4,
CO2, and N2O. NH3 was trapped in a sulfuric acid solution
and then measured by titration with a sodium hydroxide solution [17].
Measurement of Solid Samples
At the end of the experiment of BSFL treatment, residue and larvae were separated and weighed. All the solid samples were air dried and then crushed for the determination of Kjeldahl nitrogen (TKN) and total organic carbon (TOC). The TKN and TOC contents were analyzed using the methods of the Chinese national standard (NY525-2012) with dried samples.
Statistical Analysis
The experimental data were analyzed by the EXCEL 2010 software and plotted by the Origin 9.0. The data from different treatments were subjected to one-way analysis of variance (ANOVA) using SPSS (SPSS Statistical IBM) 20.0. P < 0.05 was considered as significantly different between the compared groups.
